ere restored in both cases; their test directories were removed. A generated known_hosts.old backup was subsequently removed, and the final workflow remained healthy. The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol and was fully verified. Final observations show no failed units, no test residue, healthy package state, and no unexpected listeners.","evidence_ids":["cmd-df3bd0e5f3904de7","cmd-f9134ff7f07c4348","cmd-de59845ce41344a2","cmd-dad0895a3c834692","cmd-e64263d738ed4ebb","cmd-125d8dabc6a94518","cmd-f87a4c1da1044251","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, systemd acknowledged the restart, the boot ID changed, and sshd, account files, pinned-key authentication, platform state, and failed-unit state recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently confirm the restart.","limitations":["One intermediate post-restart whole-file PIN_MATCH display was blank because the known_hosts file contained multiple legitimate server keys; a corrected comparison directly confirmed the pinned ED25519 key, and subsequent mismatch and successful-connection tests resolved the ambiguity."]}
